<section id="why">
<h2>Why we built it</h2>
<p>Most compliance and product teams look for an identity verification or AML vendor only once every few years. By then the market has moved. New providers have launched, others have been bought, prices have changed and every website promises global coverage, high pass rates and fast onboarding.</p>
<p>Sorting that out usually means a stack of sales calls, analyst reports behind a paywall and comparison pages written by the vendors themselves. We wanted one place where the basic facts sit next to each other: what a provider does, where it works, what it costs if that is public, which certifications it holds and who it suits.</p>
<p>So in 2021 we started collecting that information in a single database. BeVerified is the public version of it.</p>
</section>

<section id="what-we-do">
<h2>What we do</h2>
<p>We review and rank providers of KYC, KYB, AML screening, liveness detection, crypto compliance and related verification software. Every review uses the same <a href="/methodology/">scoring rubric</a>, and every fact on a review is labelled with where it came from: the vendor's own documents, a public register, an independent test or a third-party report.</p>
<p>You can browse providers <a href="/use-cases/">by use case</a>, <a href="/regions/">by country</a> or <a href="/providers/">A to Z</a>. We re-check reviews on a schedule, and the "Last verified" date on each one only changes after a real re-check.</p>
</section>

<section id="what-we-dont-do">
<h2>What we don't do</h2>
<ul>
<li>We don't verify identities or businesses, and we don't run background checks. We compare the companies that do.</li>
<li>We aren't connected to BeenVerified, the US people-search service. The names are similar; the businesses are not related.</li>
<li>We don't sell scores, rankings or reviews. A provider can't pay to move up a list.</li>
<li>We don't give legal or compliance advice. Our reviews help you build a shortlist; the final decision should involve your own due diligence.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section id="money">
<h2>How we stay independent</h2>
<p>Some links on the site may earn us a commission if you sign up with a provider. That money never changes a score or the order of a ranking, and providers that pay us nothing are reviewed the same way as everyone else. The full policy is in our <a href="/methodology/#disclosure">methodology</a>.</p>
</section>

<section id="team">
<h2>Who is behind it</h2>
<p>Reviews are written and edited by <a href="/authors/andrii-klymenko/">Andrii Klymenko</a>, who checks vendor claims against public registers, pricing pages and independent test results before a score goes live.</p>
</section>

